  "notes": "Entirely business-type entity (housing authority). All statements have Enterprise Funds, Component Unit (Shady Bend Villas, LLC) and Total columns; the Enterprise Funds column (primary government) is used throughout, excluding the discretely presented component unit, a separate legal entity (Total column incl. the CU: receipts 6,836,681, expenses 7,123,780, net position 13,668,699 -> 14,609,080, total assets 16,720,344). The printed Enterprise Funds Total Noncurrent Assets omits the 5,337 right-of-use asset, so printed total assets 14,210,151 do not foot (lines 14,215,488 = 1,297,451 + 12,918,037); recorded in report_discrepancies. Capital Contributions - HUD 1,227,480 recorded as business_type.other_financing (not a receipt). Interest income is printed in operating revenue. Change in Unrealized Gains 11,697 (nonoperating) recorded as investment income; interest expense 3,755 as disbursement. No single printed total for revenues/expenses so reported_totals are computed (operating + nonoperating). Net position roll: 11,826,847 + 6,669,043 - 6,805,333 + 1,227,480 = 12,918,037. Cash flow statement Enterprise Funds column used; noncapital financing section not present. Restricted cash and accrued real estate tax are '-' in the Enterprise column and omitted. No detail schedules in trimmed PDF. Trimmed p5 (gained in v7 re-trim, report p13) is the cash flow reconciliation of operating loss and supplementary disclosure; nothing new to add. Read pages 1-5 of 5",
